<title>UK: Hewden-Stuart buys Kvaerner UK unit.</title>
<headline>Hewden-Stuart buys Kvaerner UK unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Glasgow-based construction equipment group Hewden-Stuart Plc said on Monday it had bought Agent Plant Group Ltd, a subsidiary of Kvaerner Plc, for 9.35 million stg cash.</p>
<p>Agent Plant is a non-operator hire company with turnover of 10 million stg for the year to September 1995.</p>
<p>It presently has 154 employees.</p>
<p>The acquisition does not include the operations of crawler cranes, tower cranes or site accomomodation, Hewden-Stuart said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
